--- a/documentation/Usage.md
+++ b/documentation/Usage.md
@@ -1565,6 +1565,37 @@ for a socket connection or
 
 for a serial connection.
 
+If the remote is not one of the predefined machines it reports the machine type UNKNOWN (0) in CMD_INIT.
+Then the memory layout has to be defined with "customMemory", in the same format as for zsim (see [customMemory](#custommemory); "ioMmu" and "filePath" are not used).
+The bank indices are the bank numbers the remote reports for the slots.
+A bank that is visible in several slots of different sizes can use "bankSize" and "bankOffset", e.g. a 16k ROM that can also be paged into two 8k slots:
+~~~json
+    "remoteType": "dzrp",
+    "dzrp": {
+        "port": 14000,
+        "customMemory": {
+            "slots": [
+                {
+                    "range": ["0x0000", "0x3FFF"],
+                    "banks": [{"index": 0, "name": "ROM", "rom": true}, {"index": 1, "name": "RAM0"}]
+                },
+                {
+                    "range": ["0x4000", "0xBFFF"],
+                    "banks": [{"index": 2, "name": "RAM1"}]
+                },
+                {
+                    "range": ["0xC000", "0xDFFF"],
+                    "banks": [{"index": 0, "bankSize": "0x4000"}, {"index": 3, "name": "RAM2"}]
+                },
+                {
+                    "range": ["0xE000", "0xFFFF"],
+                    "banks": [{"index": 0, "bankSize": "0x4000", "bankOffset": "0x2000"}, {"index": 4, "name": "RAM3"}]
+                }
+            ]
+        }
+    }
+~~~
+
 
